No signal mask saved by the jumps of s7_call and the like (TeXmacs)

s7 saves the place to jump to on an error, throw or call-with-exit with
sigsetjmp (buf, 1) in set_jump_info, at each s7_call, s7_read,
s7_load... Saving the signal mask is a system call (sigprocmask): about
10% of the time of the external scanners of tree-sitter, which C calls
for nearly every token. These jumps never leave a signal handler (the
only one which does, siglet of s7_is_valid for SIGSEGV, keeps its mask),
so the mask is the same when they jump as when it was saved, and there
is nothing to restore: savemask 0. On Windows s7 uses setjmp, which
saves no mask either. Parses with a Scheme scanner were 7 to 10% faster.

--- a/s7.c
+++ b/s7.c
@@ -32131,11 +32131,14 @@
       LongJmp(*(Sc->Goto_Start), Error_Jump);	\
   } while (0)
 
+/* TeXmacs: no signal mask saved (savemask 0): these jumps never leave a
+ *   signal handler, and saving the mask is a system call at each s7_call
+ */
 #define set_jump_info(Sc, Tag)			\
   do {						\
     Sc->longjmp_ok = true;			\
     Sc->setjmp_loc = Tag;			\
-    jump_loc = (jump_loc_t)SetJmp(new_goto_start, 1);	\
+    jump_loc = (jump_loc_t)SetJmp(new_goto_start, 0);	\
     Sc->Goto_Start = &new_goto_start;		\
   } while (0)
 
